 is kept. INTERIOR: 164 disagreeing interior pixels out of 673,455,908 over 201 seeded draws of 64 states at the shipped supersample 1, all inside the cart or pole capsule and all off by exactly 1/255; the count is IDENTICAL at supersample 2 and unchanged at supersample 4, so it is the per-vertex/per-pixel shading difference above and not a coverage rule. The worst single draw is 0.9999988, and the floor is set to 0.99999, which is 8.4x inside it.", "state_dim": 0, "default_size": 240, "state_names": [], "step_reference_exact": null, "step_reference_control": null, "step_reference_gate": null, "class": "MujocoInvertedPendulum", "module": "stable_envs.envs.mujoco_locomotion", "doc": "Gymnasium InvertedPendulum-v5. State is qpos; the frame is a measured pure function of it, and the camera gymnasium freezes at the first render is carried in the style.", "has_step": false, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["nvdiff", "raycast3d"]}, "MujocoInvertedDoublePendulum": {"name": "mujoco-inverted-double-pendulum", "reference_id": "gymnasium/InvertedDoublePendulum-v5", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 1.0, "parity_note": "MOVER-PIXEL PARITY (supersample 1, against gymnasium at MuJoCo's default offsamples=4, 240 px, 32 states per env). The plate is baked through MuJoCo itself, so every static pixel is the reference's own rasterization and non-mover pixels are 99.76-99.93% bit-identical; the whole residual is inside the moving primitives, which are 0.3-4.4% of the frame. There the shader reaches 3-32% of pixels exact and 37-67% within 1/255 (mean 2.5-7.7/255), and on mover pixels eroded by one \u2014 so coverage is not in play \u2014 6-34% exact and 53-72% within 1/255 (mean 2.2-3.9/255). THOSE MOVER NUMBERS ARE THE PRICE OF ss=1 AND ARE STATED AS SUCH: at supersample 2 the identical protocol gives 16-35% / 64-78% (mean 2.0-3.1) and 20-37% / 67-88% (mean 1.3-2.0). None of it reaches an as