nt", "class": "SimplePointMaze", "module": "stable_envs.envs.simple_point_maze", "doc": "``swm/SimplePointMaze-v0`` with ``show_goal=False``. State: the agent's ``(x, y)`` in a 5x5 box.", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": ["scene"]}, "TwoRoom": {"name": "swm-two-room", "reference_id": "swm/TwoRoom-v1", "fidelity_tier": "parity", "render_decoder": "renderer", "visual_fidelity": {}, "visual_note": "", "parity_interior_min": 0.999995, "parity_note": "1 ulp of exp, not geometry. Run on the CPU with the reference's own float32 exp this renderer reproduces the official frame BIT FOR BIT and the device contributes nothing (measured both ways); the residual is entirely that our exp is correctly rounded and torch's CPU float32 exp is only faithful. That ulp changes a pixel only where the dot's colour equals the background, because 255*(1-a)+255*a is the identity in exact arithmetic and not in float32, and the 41 px Gaussian tail is flat enough that the reference's own 3x3 neighbourhood cannot see the quantisation contour. Worst of 800 seeded draws: 2 pixels of 2.3 million, 1/255, one channel. See the module docstring.", "state_dim": 2, "default_size": 224, "state_names": ["agent_x", "agent_y"], "step_reference_exact": true, "step_reference_control": "agent", "step_reference_gate": "agent", "class": "TwoRoom", "module": "stable_envs.envs.swm_nav", "doc": "``swm/TwoRoom-v1`` at its shipped appearance: two rooms, a wall with doors, no target drawn.\n\nState is the agent position and nothing else, because that is all the frame reads under\n``render_target = 0``. The goal image a swm workflow consumes is not a second kind of frame \u2014 the\nofficial env produces it as ``_render_frame(agent_pos=target_position)``, i.e. this same renderer\nat a different state \u2014 so a corpus of agent positions regenerates the goals too.", "has_step": true, "render_overridden": true, "backends": []}, "TwoRoomTarget": {"name": "swm-two-room-target", "reference_id": "swm/T